'''''Lonicera implexa''''', sometimes known by the common but nonspecific names '''Minorca''', '''evergreen or Mediterranean honeysuckle''', is a species of flowering plants in the [[Caprifoliaceae]] family.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Lonicera implexa {{!}} Minorca honeysuckle /RHS |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/10476/lonicera-implexa/details |access-date=2025-02-21 |website=www.rhs.org.uk |language=en-gb}}</ref><ref name=":1" /> As with most ''Lonicera'' (honeysuckle) species, ''L. implexa'' is a climbing plant growing to 2.5 m or more.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lonicera implexa Soland. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/7019976|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref>

''Lonicera implexa'' is native to the Mediterranean region. In southern Europe, it can be found along the entire European Mediterranean region, with its native range includes Portugal and Spain (including the Balearic islands), southern France (including Corsica), Italy (including Sardinia and Sicily), Malta,<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Lonicera implexa (Evergreen Honeysuckle) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/CAPR/Lonicera_implexa.php |access-date=2022-03-05 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref> Western Balkans, Greece (including East Aegean islands) and the European part of Turkey (East Thrace). In northern Africa, its range is limited to the Mediterranean region of Morocco, Algeria and Tunisia.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lonicera implexa Aiton {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:148839-1 |access-date=2025-02-21 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Lonicera implexa Aiton |url=https://www.worldfloraonline.org/taxon/wfo-0000359592 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230407221516/http://www.worldfloraonline.org/taxon/wfo-0000359592 |archive-date=2023-04-07 |access-date=2025-02-21 |website=www.worldfloraonline.org |language=en}}</ref>

''Lonicera implexa'' is sometimes cultivated as a garden plant outside of its native range,<ref name=":0" /> having been first introduced to the United Kingdom in 1772.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lonicera implexa - Trees and Shrubs Online |url=https://www.treesandshrubsonline.org/articles/lonicera/lonicera-implexa/ |access-date=2025-02-21 |website=www.treesandshrubsonline.org}}</ref>

